    "_note": "The Shaft as the player inherits it: [buildingId, level] pairs, placed and fully staffed through the same commands the player uses, so the opening lands in the command log and replays with everything else. Level 1 was built before anyone alive: the auditorium and the Exit carry a fixed block in the catalogue and go only where it says. Cultivation sits high and the canteens low, so food is hauled a long way down — which is what puts porters on the stairwell where they can be watched. porters: each hired at the named station and given the route, stops naming [buildingId, level, nth] — nth counts that building on that level in placement order (0 when omitted); each stop picks up or drops off one good, `qty` per visit or all. links: the cables, wires, pipes, drains, feed lines and ducts the Shaft opens with, each naming its two ends as [buildingId, level, nth] and plugged into the first free sockets that fit (catalog/infrastructure/networks.json); an entry with a `name` may be teed into by a later one that gives `tap` (that name) instead of `to` — every room that draws power is wired to a junction and every room that uses water is fed from a cistern; priorities: junction priorities, 1 served first, others left at the default. fans: which way each duct fan turns, suck or blow (a fan not named blows).",
